{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1502312046,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExOTk4NTE4NjA="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1502324141,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTIwMDA3OTczNA=="},"title":"save submodule    does not commit modified submodule ","was":"save submodule    does not commit modified submodule "},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502446420,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTIwMjM1Mzg0NA=="},"added":[],"removed":["severity-normal"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502447154,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyMTc3ODUzNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1700#issuecomment-321778536"},"message":"This is not a bug. At least not a bug in the code.\n\nThe reason for this behavior is this: Most commands eat an arbitrary number of paths. `save` will take any paths and save them. If you don't say what to save into, it will save whatever is necessary to make anything that you gave as a path argument to be clean at the end. So in your case, it finds `workshops` to be clean, and informs you about it.\n\nThis following commands would all do the job:\n\n```\ndatalad save\ndatalad save .\ndatalad save -d . -m \"Added initial subdataset with sherlock for MIND-2017\" workshops\ndatalad save -S workshops\n```\n\nIn `dev-master` `--all-updated` is the default behavior -- it won't touch untracked content unless given as an explicit path.\n\nPS: While everything I said above is true, I just found, while lecturing you, that `-S` in addition does things that it should not do. I guess I deserve that....","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1502463666,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEyMDI3NjAwODU="},"added":["for our information"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1503992842,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNTU4Mjg3MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1700#issuecomment-325582871"},"message":"This is on record now. Closing.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1503992842,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTIyNTA5NTQ2OA=="},"status":2}]}